{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "import dataclasses\nfrom typing import List, Tuple as TypingTuple, Union\n\n\n@dataclasses.dataclass\nclass Tuple:\n    elements: List[int]\n\n\n@dataclasses.dataclass\nclass TupleList:\n    tuples: List[Tuple]\n\n\n@dataclasses.dataclass\nclass ResultList:\n    tuples: List[Tuple]\n\n\ndef find_tuples(tuple_list: TupleList | list[TypingTuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> ResultList:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples where all elements are divisible by k.\n    The function accepts either a TupleList dataclass or a plain list of built-in tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    result_tuples = []\n\n    # Unify input to iterate over built-in tuples\n    if isinstance(tuple_list, TupleList):\n        input_tuples_raw = [tuple(t.elements) for t in tuple_list.tuples]\n    else:\n        input_tuples_raw = tuple_list\n\n    for current_tuple in input_tuples_raw:\n        all_elements_divisible = True\n        for element in current_tuple:\n            if element % k != 0:\n                all_elements_divisible = False\n                break\n        if all_elements_divisible:\n            result_tuples.append(Tuple(elements=list(current_tuple)))\n            \n    return ResultList(tuples=result_tuples)"}
