{"task_id": "Mbpp/413", "solution": "def extract_nth_element(list_of_tuples, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract the 0-based n-th element from each tuple in list_of_tuples.\n\n    Returns a list preserving the order of input tuples. Raises IndexError if any tuple is missing the index n.\n    Raises TypeError if arguments fail validation (list_of_tuples not iterable of tuples or n not int).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Index 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    if not hasattr(list_of_tuples, '__iter__'):\n        raise TypeError(\"First argument 'list_of_tuples' must be an iterable.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for item in list_of_tuples:\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(\"Elements in 'list_of_tuples' must be tuples.\")\n        result.append(item[n])\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef max_Product(integers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds a pair of integers from the input list with the highest product.\n    Returns the pair as a tuple, ordered smallest to largest.\"\"\"\n\n    # Initialize variables to track the two largest and two smallest numbers.\n    # These will be updated to hold actual numbers from the list if present.\n    max1 = float('-inf')  # Largest number found\n    max2 = float('-inf')  # Second largest number found\n    min1 = float('inf')   # Smallest number found (most negative)\n    min2 = float('inf')   # Second smallest number found\n\n    for num in integers:\n        # Update largest numbers\n        if num > max1:\n            max2 = max1\n            max1 = num\n        elif num > max2:\n            max2 = num\n\n        # Update smallest numbers\n        if num < min1:\n            min2 = min1\n            min1 = num\n        elif num < min2:\n            min2 = num\n\n    # Calculate products of potential candidate pairs.\n    # The two largest numbers (e.g., 7*8 = 56)\n    prod_largest_pair = max1 * max2\n\n    # The two smallest numbers (useful if both are negative, e.g., -10*-5 = 50)\n    prod_smallest_pair = min1 * min2\n\n    # Determine which pair yields the maximum product and return them in sorted order.\n    if prod_largest_pair >= prod_smallest_pair:\n        return (min(max1, max2), max(max1, max2))\n    else:\n        return (min(min1, min2), max(min1, min2))"}
