{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def binary_search_right(list, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a binary search to find the right insertion point (upper bound).\n    Returns the index where value should be inserted to maintain sorted order\n    and place duplicates to the right.\n    \"\"\"\n    left = 0\n    right = len(list)\n\n    while left < right:\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\n        if list[mid] <= value:\n            left = mid + 1\n        else:\n            right = mid\n    return left\n\ndef right_insertion(list, value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in sorted order.\n    For duplicates, returns the index immediately after the last equal element.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list:\n        return 0\n    \n    return binary_search_right(list, value)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/788", "solution": "def new_tuple(list: list, string: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Create and return a tuple composed of the input list elements (in order) followed by the input string.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the first argument is not a list or the second argument is not a str.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"First argument must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Second argument must be a str.\")\n\n    return tuple(list) + (string,)"}
